From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [TargetParser] Keep aarch64 in the process triple of an ILP32
 process

sys::getProcessTriple() replaces a 64-bit architecture with its 32-bit
variant when pointers are 4 bytes wide. For an AArch64 ILP32 host
(aarch64-*-linux-gnu_ilp32 or -musl_ilp32) that turns the triple into
arm-*, another instruction set, and every JIT that starts from the
process triple fails with

  No available targets are compatible with triple "arm-unknown-linux-musl_ilp32"

The architecture of an ILP32 process is still aarch64: leave it.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 llvm/lib/TargetParser/Host.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Host.cpp b/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Host.cpp
index 8fd91fcd3..3bff129a0 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Host.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/TargetParser/Host.cpp
@@ -2325,7 +2325,10 @@ std::string sys::getProcessTriple() {
 
   if (sizeof(void *) == 8 && PT.isArch32Bit())
     PT = PT.get64BitArchVariant();
-  if (sizeof(void *) == 4 && PT.isArch64Bit())
+  // An AArch64 ILP32 process has 32-bit pointers, but its architecture is
+  // still aarch64: the 32-bit variant, arm, is another instruction set.
+  if (sizeof(void *) == 4 && PT.isArch64Bit() &&
+      !(PT.isAArch64() && PT.isILP32Environment()))
     PT = PT.get32BitArchVariant();
 
   return PT.str();
